    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n1. **Added named exports for governance constants** (`src/finetune/index.js`): The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports while keeping the default export intact for backward compatibility.\n\n2. **Fixed toxicityMetric function signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`): The `toxicityMetric` was being called with `(outputs, references)` from `runEvaluations`, but it expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. This caused the references array to be incorrectly interpreted as banned terms, flagging legitimate outputs. I updated the signature to accept `references` as the second parameter (which it ignores) so it uses the default banned terms correctly.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, and the changes maintain backward compatibility with existing public exports.",
